🚁 DIY Fighter Helicopter Model (Arduino-Based)

Complete Project Journal

Project Name: DIY Fighter Helicopter Model (Arduino-Based)

Total Project Time: 29 Hours

Journal Parts: 5

---

Part 1 – Project Planning and Design (5 Hours)

Objective

Research different fighter helicopter designs, prepare the project plan, select materials, and create the initial sketch.

Activities Performed

- Researched real fighter helicopter designs.
- Prepared the project sketch and dimensions.
- Selected Arduino and electronic components.
- Listed all required materials and tools.
- Planned the project timeline and organized the workspace.

Challenges Faced

- Choosing a simple yet realistic helicopter design.
- Selecting lightweight but strong construction materials.

Outcome

A complete project plan, design sketch, and material list were prepared.

---

Part 2 – Frame Assembly (6 Hours)

Objective

Construct the main helicopter body and supporting frame.

Activities Performed

- Cut foam board according to measurements.
- Built the cockpit and tail section.
- Installed landing skids.
- Mounted rotor supports.
- Reinforced the frame for better strength.

Challenges Faced

- Maintaining body symmetry.
- Keeping the model lightweight.

Outcome

A strong and realistic helicopter frame was completed.

---

Part 3 – Electronics Installation (6 Hours)

Objective

Install Arduino and electronic components.

Activities Performed

- Installed Arduino Uno.
- Mounted the DC motor.
- Connected LEDs and battery.
- Completed all wiring.
- Tested electrical connections.

Challenges Faced

- Organizing wires inside the helicopter body.
- Balancing the weight of electronic components.

Outcome

All electronics were installed successfully.

---

Part 4 – Programming and Testing (6 Hours)

Objective

Upload Arduino code and verify hardware functionality.

Activities Performed

- Uploaded the Arduino program.
- Tested the DC motor.
- Verified LED operation.
- Checked wiring using a multimeter.
- Fixed minor connection issues and optimized the system.

Challenges Faced

- Rotor balancing.
- Loose wire connections during testing.

Outcome

The helicopter operated successfully with a rotating rotor and working LEDs.

---

Part 5 – Final Assembly and Documentation (6 Hours)

Objective

Complete the helicopter model and prepare all documentation.

Activities Performed

- Completed final assembly.
- Cleaned and finished the exterior.
- Performed final functional testing.
- Prepared the README, BOM, diagrams, and Arduino code.
- Captured project photographs and organized the GitHub repository.

Challenges Faced

- Ensuring a professional finish.
- Verifying all documentation before submission.

Outcome

The DIY Fighter Helicopter Model was successfully completed and prepared for demonstration and GitHub submission.

---

Skills Learned

- Arduino Programming
- Hardware Assembly
